# Line endings: normalize to LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# The repository is developed on Windows and CI runs on Linux and macOS, so a
# file's ending depended on whoever last saved it: one tracked file (webui/ws.go)
# was committed as CRLF and two design docs had a mixed file, which made gofmt
# report them dirty on every machine and turned any edit into a whole-file
# rewrite. Declaring the policy here makes the checkout identical everywhere and
# keeps a future contribution from reintroducing the drift.
#
# No tracked file is binary (checked: `git ls-files` holds only Go, Markdown,
# JS/CSS/HTML/SVG, YAML, Makefile, LICENSE and Dockerfile), so every file can be
# treated as text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly text so a future `* text=auto` change cannot silently make these
# binary, which would disable diffs for the files that most need reviewing.
*.go    text
*.md    text
*.js    text
*.css   text
*.html  text
*.svg   text
*.yml   text
*.json  text
*.mod   text
*.sum   text

Makefile    text
Dockerfile  text
LICENSE     text
.gitignore  text
